CC0 1.0 Universal — Public Domain Dedication
============================================

The sample corpus in this directory — the seed photograph `_seed/river.jpg` and
every file generated from it under `RG-*/UC-*/files/` — is dedicated to the
public domain under Creative Commons CC0 1.0 Universal.

To the extent possible under law, Pascal Menardais has waived all copyright and
related or neighbouring rights to this corpus. You may copy, modify, distribute
and use it, including for commercial purposes, without asking permission.

Full legal code: https://creativecommons.org/publicdomain/zero/1.0/legalcode

Why CC0 and not MIT
-------------------
MIT is a software licence; it fits the code in this repository, not a
photograph. CC0 is the usual instrument for releasing media into the public
domain, and it removes any doubt about reusing the corpus in a downstream
test suite.

Provenance
----------
`_seed/river.jpg` is an original photograph by the author. Every other file in
this corpus is derived from it or forged byte by byte by
`tools/build_samples.py`. No third-party content is included, so the corpus can
be redistributed without further attribution obligations.

The source code of this project remains under the MIT licence — see ../LICENSE.
